From fd8055e6cd041cc8a13ca99a9763767437994680 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: proshiv85-byte <proshiv85@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:15:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 18/25] WIP: media: s5p-mfc: add MFC v11 (Exynos8895)

The Exynos8895 MFC (Samsung's "v11", version register 0x1100) has the
v10 interface and formats. Variant with the vendor kernel's context
buffer sizes and the firmware as s5p-mfc-v11.fw (mfc_fw.bin of the
vendor partition). Fixes needed on top of the v10 support:

- the bus reset is left set (by the bootloader, or by the reset done
  on an earlier failure) and the MFC reset does not release it: the
  firmware could not be fetched. Release it after the reset (v10/v11).
- the firmware has to be reloaded for every run, as on v12, or
  SYS_INIT fails the second time.
- H.264 MV buffers need the 1024 byte offset (as on v12): INIT_BUFFERS
  failed with error 0x3c.
- the stream buffer must be at least 1 MiB: smaller ones, which FFmpeg
  allocates for small videos, fail header parsing (error 0x37).
- on v10+ the buffer holding the header is kept when the header is
  followed by a frame, for all codecs and not only H.264: HEVC, VP8 and
  VP9 lost their first keyframe.
- timestamps are also copied for frames decoded but displayed later
  (reordering), which got none; FFmpeg users like Firefox gave up.
- NV12 in a single buffer (chroma at bytesperline * height) as decoder
  output on v10+, listed first: Firefox's V4L2 support only takes it.

Verified with FFmpeg's *_v4l2m2m decoders: H.264, HEVC, VP8 and VP9
output is identical to software decoding, 320x240 to 1080p; 1080p
H.264 decodes at ~245 fps with ~18% of one CPU.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
